        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Fix Windows command not found detection in tool-handlers.ts",
        "summary": "Added Windows-specific error string 'is not recognized as an internal or external command' to the 'command not found' detection logic in `npm-app/src/tool-handlers.ts`. This ensures `handleRunTerminalCommand` correctly identifies failed commands on Windows, preventing false negatives when checking for syntax or not-found errors. Scope limited to `npm-app` core tool handlers.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:20:23.645Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you ask the assistant to run a command in a terminal on a Windows computer, it now correctly recognizes when Windows says the command doesn\\'t exist. Previously, a Windows message like \\\"not recognized as an internal or external command\\\" could be missed, making the assistant think the command succeeded or had a different problem. Now it treats that message as a \\\"command not found\\\" error, so it can respond appropriately instead of getting confused.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
