        "v": 5,
        "title": "Refactor skipped terminal commands in CLI",
        "summary": "Refactors `skippedTerminalCommands` in `npm-app/src/cli.ts` to dynamically append trailing spaces to base command strings ('what', 'which', 'file'). This change centralizes the formatting logic, improving maintainability while preserving existing behavior for terminal command skipping.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:20:16.929Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the tool decides whether to skip running a command in your terminal, it now builds its list of commands to skip (such as 'what', 'which', and 'file') in one place instead of writing each one out separately. This makes the code easier to maintain but does not change how skipping works. As a result, behavior stays the same for internal tooling that relies on this skipping logic. The change was released as part of version 1.0.51 alongside a fix for command-not-found detection on Windows.",
